M, Sim JH. Evolution of bioethics education in the medical programme: A tale of two medical schools? Int J Ethics Educ. 2020:1–4. doi: 10.1007/s40889-020-00112-0. [ Google Scholar ] 20. D’Souza RF, Mathew M, D’Souza DS, Palatty P. Novel horizontal and vertical integrated bioethics curriculum for medical courses. Med Teach. 2018;40:573–7. doi: 10.1080/0142159X.2018.1442921. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Ngan OM, Sim JH. Evolution of bioethics education in the medical programme: A tale of two medical schools? Int J Ethics Educ. 2020:1–4. doi: 10.1007/s40889-020-00112-0. [ Google Scholar ] 22. Narinasamy I, Logeswaran AK. Teacher as moral model – Are we caring enough? World J Educ. 2015;5:1–13. [ Google Scholar ] 23. Nalini A. The significance of the hidden curriculum in medical ethics: Literature review with focus on students'' experiences? Int J User Driven Healthc (IJUDH) 2013;3:1–12. doi: 10.4018/ijudh.2013100101. [ Google Scholar ] 24. Wolf SM. Introduction: Gender and feminism in bioethics: Beyond reproduction. In: Wolf SM, editor. Feminism & Bioethics: Beyond Reproduction. Minnesota, USA: Oxford University Press; 1996. pp. 3–43. [ Google Scholar ] 25. Spilker K, Lie M. Gender and bioethics intertwined: Egg donation within the context of equal opportunities. Eur J Womens Stud. 2007;14:327–40. [ Google Scholar ] 26. Annas GJ. A national bill of patients'' rights. N Engl J Med. 1998;338:695–9. doi: 10.1056/NEJM199803053381020. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Ghodsi Z, Hojjatoleslami S. Knowledge of students about patient rights and its relationship with some factors in Iran. Procedia Soc Behav Sci. 2012;31:345–8. [ Google Scholar ] 28. Al Anazi BD, Faraj F, Al Balawi MM, Al Anazi MD. The awareness of patients'' bill of rights among medical interns and medical students at Tabuk University. Open Access Maced J Med Sci. 2019;7:2932–9. doi: 10.3889/oamjms.2019.785. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. Sullivan M. The new 