ating with Muslim parents: “The Four Principles” are not as culturally neutral as suggested. Eur J Pediatr. 2009;168:1383–7. doi: 10.1007/s00431-009-0970-8. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 94. Witter RA, Stock WA, Okun MA, Haring MJ. Religion and subjective well-being in adulthood: A quantitative synthesis. Rev Relig Res. 1985;26:332–42. [ Google Scholar ] 95. Zeng Y, Shen K. Resilience significantly contributes to exceptional longevity. Curr Gerontol Geriatr Res 2010. 2010:525693. doi: 10.1155/2010/525693. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Suggested Reading/Viewing 1. APA 1998 Annual Report. The President''s Address. Martin E. P. Seligman. Positive Psychology Center. [Last accessed on 2014 Mar 30]. Available from: http://www.ppc.sas.upenn.edu/aparep98.htm . 2. American Psychiatric Association. The Principles of Medical Ethics with Annotations Especially Applicable to Psychiatry. 2013 Edition; 2013. [Last accessed on 2014 Mar 30]. Available from: http://www.file:///C:/Documents%20and%20Settings/user/My%20Documents/Downloads/principles2013-final.pdf . 3. John-Stewart G. Bioethics. Internet Encyclopedia of Philosophy: A Peer Reviewed Academic Resource. [Last accessed on 2014 Mar 30]. Available from: http://www.iep.utm.edu/bioethic/ 4. Jeste D. APA President Dilip Jeste, MD, Explains Positive Psychiatry – Video Interview. [Last accessed on 2014 Mar 30]. Available from: http://www.psychcongress.com/video/breaking-news-apa-president-dilip-jeste-md-explains-positive-psychiatry-video-interview-11554 . 5. Jeste DV. Positive Psychiatry. From the President. 15 June, 2012. [Last accessed on 2014 Mar 30]. Available from: http://www.psychnews.psychiatryonline.org/newsarticle.aspx?articleid=1182477 . 6. Marcum JA. Philosophy of Medicine. Internet Encyclopedia of Philosophy: A Peer Reviewed Academic Resource. [Last accessed on 2014 Mar 30]. Available from: http://www.iep.utm.edu/medicine/#H3 . 7. Wikipedia. Bioethics. [Last acces